## Task 2: Dockerfile Verification
The Dockerfile uses Node.js LTS and builds the application container.

Main Dockerfile steps:

```dockerfile
FROM node:20-alpine
WORKDIR /app
COPY package*.json ./
RUN npm ci
COPY backend/package*.json ./backend/
RUN cd backend && npm ci --omit=dev
COPY backend ./backend
COPY frontend ./frontend
RUN npm test
ENV PORT=5000
EXPOSE 5000
CMD ["npm", "start"]
```

The Dockerfile installs the root assignment dependencies and the backend dependencies before starting the backend server.

## Task 3: GitHub Actions Workflow
The deployment workflow is saved in:

```text
../.github/workflows/deploy.yml
```

GitHub Actions reads workflows from the repository-root `.github/workflows` folder, so this root workflow is the one that runs after pushing to GitHub.

The workflow also has a copy in:

```text
.github/workflows/deploy.yml
```

Workflow stages:

1. Checkout the repository.
2. Login to DockerHub.
3. Build the Docker image from the `A1` folder.
4. Push the image to DockerHub.
5. Trigger Render deployment through a Render deploy webhook.

Workflow summary:

```yaml
name: Docker Build and Render Deploy

on:
  push:
    branches:
      - main
  workflow_dispatch:

env:
  IMAGE_NAME: todo-app

jobs:
  build-and-deploy:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest

    steps:
      - name: Checkout Repository
        uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Login to DockerHub
        uses: docker/login-action@v3
        with:
          username: ${{ secrets.DOCKERHUB_USERNAME }}
          password: ${{ secrets.DOCKERHUB_TOKEN }}

      - name: Build and Push Docker Image
        run: |
          docker build -t ${{ secrets.DOCKERHUB_USERNAME }}/${{ env.IMAGE_NAME }}:latest ./A1
          docker push ${{ secrets.DOCKERHUB_USERNAME }}/${{ env.IMAGE_NAME }}:latest

      - name: Trigger Render Deployment
        run: curl --fail --request POST "${{ secrets.RENDER_DEPLOY_HOOK_URL }}"
```

## Required GitHub Secrets
The following secrets must be added in GitHub before running the workflow:

| Secret Name | Description |
|---|---|
| `DOCKERHUB_USERNAME` | DockerHub username |
| `DOCKERHUB_TOKEN` | DockerHub access token |
| `RENDER_DEPLOY_HOOK_URL` | Render deploy hook URL |

Credentials are stored in GitHub Secrets and are not hardcoded in the project.

## Task 4: Render Deployment
On Render.com, create a new web service and select the option to deploy from an existing Docker image.

Docker image format:

```text
<dockerhub-username>/todo-app:latest
```

After each push to the `main` branch, GitHub Actions builds and pushes the latest Docker image. The final workflow step calls the Render deploy hook so Render redeploys the latest image.

